  "version": 1,
  "name": "Liquor-Log flavour wheel",
  "provenance": "Own work. Descriptors are the ordinary sensory vocabulary in common use and are not owned by anyone. The grouping is by ORIGIN - where the flavour comes from in the grain, the ferment, the still or the barrel - which is a chemical and process fact rather than a copy of any published wheel's arrangement. Sub-groups within a family are presentational only. See docs/06-flavour-wheel-provenance.md.",
